<title>PHILIPPINES: Benpres sets yields debt issue.</title>
<headline>Benpres sets yields debt issue.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Benpres Holdings Corp said on Thursday that the yield for its issue of five-year debt paper would be set at 1.0 percent over the prevailing rate for the Philippines' 91-day treasury bill.</p>
<p>It said the yield for its seven-year paper would be 1.125 percent over the 91-day T-bill rate.  </p>
<p>Benpres vice president Rafael Andrade said his company will start issuing the papers to the public on Thursday.</p>
<p>Lead underwriters of the flotation are Philippine Commercial Capital Inc and FEB Investments Inc.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
</text>
